# {{.ArtifactID}}: Piperoom reference project

The smallest Debezium Engine application for this pipeline: a {{.SourceTitle}} source on
Debezium {{.Release}}, built with {{.BuildTitle}}, Java {{.JavaRelease}} or later. Piperoom
generated it and never builds or runs it. Compare its build file with yours: the versions here
are the ones Debezium {{.Release}} was released with.

## Run it

1. Set the database password in the environment (it is never written to a file):
   `PIPEROOM_SECRET_{{.PasswordSecret}}=<password>`
2. Build: `{{.BuildCommand}}`
3. Run, from this folder: `{{.RunCommand}}`{{if .RunCommandWindows}} (Windows: `{{.RunCommandWindows}}`){{end}}

Every change event prints one line that starts with `piperoom-reference event`. Save the output
to a file (for example `piperoom-reference.log`) and give Piperoom its path: the setup check
looks for its canary in that file.

Offsets{{if eq .Source "mysql"}} and the schema history{{end}} are kept under `data/`; delete that
folder to start again with a new snapshot.
{{- if eq .Source "postgres"}}

The engine creates the replication slot `{{.SlotName}}` and the publication
`{{.PublicationName}}`. When you no longer need it, drop both, or the slot keeps WAL on the server:
`SELECT pg_drop_replication_slot('{{.SlotName}}'); DROP PUBLICATION {{.PublicationName}};`
{{- end}}
